--! Diagnostic sessions (`docs/design/webgpu.md` §6.4): the device's native
--! error scopes, pushed and popped by hand, with no unchecked handle and no
--! way around the engine's checks.
--!
--! `run` takes the device's diagnostic **lease** at once, or is refused: a
--! session never waits for one. While the lease is held, every ordinary
--! checked operation on the device — from the session's own callback, from
--! a fiber it starts or joins, or from any other fiber — returns
--! `InvalidInput (SessionState DeviceLeased)` at once. Only the forwarding
--! calls of the `Gpu.Diagnostics.*` modules, which take the session as
--! their first argument, run on the device then. They run under the
--! session's scopes: what they make is provisional, usable by the session,
--! and accepted only when the session ends with no error reported. What
--! makes no error scope runs as usual under a lease: teardown (`destroy`,
--! `unmap`, `unconfigure`), reads of state (`features`, `limits`, `label`,
--! `mapState`, `currentMapping`, `loss`, …), mapped memory
--! (`getMappedRange`, `Gpu.MappedRange`), and waits on work issued before
--! (`Gpu.Submission.done`, a pending `map`, `awaitLost`, `eachEvent`,
--! `onEvent`).
--!
--! **The livelock hazard is the program's.** A session that waits for a
--! fiber which retries an ordinary call on the leased device until it
--! succeeds never ends: the retry needs the lease to end, and the lease
--! needs the callback to return. The engine cannot see that cycle. Work a
--! session waits for must not touch the leased device through ordinary
--! calls: route it through the session, or do it after the session ends.
--!
--!     probe : Gpu.Handle.Device, Gpu.Types.SamplerDescriptor
--!         → Result Gpu.Error.Error (Gpu.Diagnostics.DiagnosticReport (Maybe Gpu.Error.GpuError))
--!     probe device descriptor =
--!         Gpu.Diagnostics.run device λsession →
--!             _ = Gpu.Diagnostics.pushErrorScope session Gpu.Types.FilterValidation
--!             _ = Gpu.Diagnostics.Device.createSampler session device descriptor
--!             case Gpu.Diagnostics.popErrorScope session of
--!                 Ok found →
--!                     found
--!
--!                 Err _ →
--!                     Nothing

import Gpu.Engine as Engine
import Gpu.Error as Error exposing (DiagnosticError, GpuError, InputError)
import Gpu.Handle as Handle
import Gpu.Types as Types
import Js
import Task


type alias V =
    Js.Value


--| What a session observed: the callback's value, `Nothing` when a scope
--| of the session reported an error — then what the session made is
--| rejected, since it may be invalid — and every error the session's own
--| scopes reported, in the order they arrived. A scope keeps one error,
--| the first of its filter: this is never a complete list.
pub type alias DiagnosticReport a =
    value : Maybe a
    observed : List GpuError


--| Run `body` with a new diagnostic session of `device`, holding the
--| device's lease until `body` returns. The lease is taken at once or
--| refused: `InvalidInput (SessionState DeviceLeased)` while a lease is
--| held, `DeviceLost` once the device's loss was observed. The session
--| pushes three scopes of its own first, which catch every error the
--| session's scopes do not. When `body` returns, is cancelled or fails,
--| every scope it left open is popped, innermost first, and the lease
--| ends, in that turn; then the run waits for the pops. An error only the
--| engine's scopes caught is the run's failure (`Validation`, …, or
--| `RelatedFailures`), and a loss observed meanwhile `DeviceLost`; what the
--| session made is then rejected. Otherwise the result is the report. A
--| cancelled run rejects what the session made. A throw in `body` is a
--| defect. May suspend; `body` may too.
pub run : Handle.Device, (Handle.DiagnosticSession → a) → Result Error.Error (DiagnosticReport a)
run device body =
    s = Engine.openSession (Js.from device) Js.null?
    within s body


--| Run `body` with a session nested in `session`, under its lease: the
--| nested session's scopes are inside the outer session's, and it ends
--| before the outer one does. While it is open, the outer session's calls
--| are `InvalidInput (SessionState DeviceLeased)`, as an ordinary call is;
--| a second nested session too. `run` called inside a session is an
--| ordinary acquisition: on the same device it is refused. The report and
--| the failures are `run`'s; what the nested session made is settled by its
--| own scopes. May suspend; `body` may too.
pub nested :
      Handle.DiagnosticSession
    , (Handle.DiagnosticSession → a)
    → Result Error.Error (DiagnosticReport a)
nested session body =
    parent = Js.from session
    s = Engine.openSession (Engine.sessionDevice parent) parent?
    within s body


within : V, (Handle.DiagnosticSession → a) → Result Error.Error (DiagnosticReport a)
within s body =
    value = Task.onExit (λ⊤ → body (Js.to s)) λexit →
        case exit of
            Task.Done _ →
                Engine.closeSession s False

            Task.Cancelled →
                Engine.closeSession s True
    errors = Engine.finishSession s?
    Ok { value = if List.isEmpty errors then Just value else Nothing, observed = errors }


--| Push a native error scope of `filter` in the session: every error of
--| that filter a later call of the session generates, until the matching
--| `popErrorScope`, goes to it, and not to a scope beneath. `SessionState
--| SessionEnded` once the session's lease ended, `DeviceLeased` while a
--| nested session of it is open. Never suspends.
pub pushErrorScope : Handle.DiagnosticSession, Types.ErrorFilter → Result InputError ⊤
pushErrorScope session filter =
    index =
        case filter of
            Types.FilterValidation →
                0

            Types.FilterOutOfMemory →
                1

            Types.FilterInternal →
                2
    Engine.pushUserScope (Js.from session) index


--| Pop the session's innermost scope and wait for what it reports: the one
--| error of its filter it kept, or `Nothing` — which is not proof that the
--| device was not lost. `ScopeUnderflow` when the session has no scope of
--| its own open: the session's own three scopes are never popped for it.
--| `SessionRefused` when the session cannot act (`pushErrorScope`'s
--| refusals). An error of a class the scope's filter does not report, or a
--| rejected pop, is a defect. May suspend.
pub popErrorScope : Handle.DiagnosticSession → Result DiagnosticError (Maybe GpuError)
popErrorScope session = Engine.popUserScope (Js.from session)


--| Whether the session can still act: `Ok` while its lease is live and no
--| nested session of it is open.
pub state : Handle.DiagnosticSession → Result Error.SessionState ⊤
state session = Engine.sessionState (Js.from session)
